<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 26 August, from 1346 to 1978.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1346 CE <span class="tih-ago">680 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward III's longbowmen defeat the French at Crécy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">English archers and dismounted men-at-arms cut down repeated French cavalry charges at Crécy. The victory, with heavy losses among the French nobility, opened the way to the siege of Calais.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1789 CE <span class="tih-ago">237 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France adopts the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The National Assembly proclaimed that men are born free and equal in rights, and that sovereignty rests with the nation. The declaration became a founding text of modern human rights.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sunda-strait.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1883 CE <span class="tih-ago">143 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Krakatoa begins its cataclysmic eruption</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The volcano of Krakatoa in the Sunda Strait began its climactic eruption, culminating in explosions the next day heard thousands of kilometres away. Tsunamis killed more than 36,000 people.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda Strait</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1920 CE <span class="tih-ago">106 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The 19th Amendment is certified, giving US women the vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secretary of State Bainbridge Colby certified the 19th Amendment, barring denial of the vote on account of sex. It crowned a campaign launched at Seneca Falls in 1848.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1978 CE <span class="tih-ago">48 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Albino Luciani is elected Pope John Paul I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Patriarch of Venice became the first pope to take a double name, honouring his two predecessors. Known as the 'smiling pope', he died after just 33 days.</p></div></li></ol>
